{"segments":[{"name":"Owner-led course businesses","buyer":"Course creator who controls the marketing budget","market":"Small businesses selling established paid courses","problem":"Testimonials are scattered when the owner updates a course sales page; validate whether a live page update creates urgent proof-collection work.","access":"Research public course sites and use published business contact routes; the owner can evaluate and purchase directly, but willingness to pay needs validation.","tradeoff":"Purchasing is simpler than a team evaluation, but infrequent launches may weaken recurring value; ask what they use today and what would justify paying."},{"name":"Small SaaS marketing teams","buyer":"Marketing lead with budget approval from the founder or finance","market":"SaaS companies maintaining product and campaign pages","problem":"Campaign teams need relevant customer proof repeatedly; validate which upcoming campaign is blocked by finding or collecting testimonials.","access":"Public company sites identify teams, but reaching the budget owner may require internal routing and a team evaluation.","tradeoff":"Recurring workflow may support stronger willingness to pay, but approval is slower; ask who approves software and which recurring proof task has a budget."},{"name":"Multi-client marketing agencies","buyer":"Agency owner or delivery director","market":"Agencies managing client websites and campaigns","problem":"Client testimonial collection delays delivery; validate whether the agency controls collection and publishing rather than merely requesting assets.","access":"Agency sites offer public contact routes, but evaluation may require both agency and client approval.","tradeoff":"Repeated client work could support payment, but permissions and workflow fit are uncertain; ask who owns the accounts and who would pay for Senja."}],"firstBuyerWhy":{"advantage":"Owner-led course businesses can evaluate Senja against a current sales-page task and authorize purchase without cross-team approval.","risk":"Launch-driven usage may not create enough recurring value to justify payment.","runnerUpWinsWhen":"Small SaaS marketing teams become preferable when a reachable budget owner confirms recurring campaign-proof work and a clear approval path."},"buyingMotion":"Sales-assisted","paymentPath":{"offerKind":"Existing SaaS","monetizationStatus":"Unknown","pricingStatementIds":[],"verify":"Inspect Senja's current official offer, paid capabilities and checkout before proposing paid conversion; s4 supports a free starting point but does not establish paid terms.","activation":"After a prospect agrees, validate a first useful event such as importing an existing testimonial into Senja for a named sales-page task.","adoption":"Observe whether the buyer returns to collect or select additional testimonials for another real marketing task.","paidConversion":"Record confirmed payment for the verified existing Senja offer, not interest, free signup or payment for assistance."},"firstExperiment":{"problem":"Test whether owner-led course businesses with a current sales-page update struggle to collect or retrieve relevant testimonials.","identifyProspects":"Use public course websites to identify owner-operated businesses, verify a relevant public observation and locate a published business contact route; ask about urgency rather than inferring it.","channel":"Direct email","channelRationale":{"decision":"Researched direct outreach can expose the owner's workflow and purchase authority without assuming existing traffic, users or community access.","tradeoff":"Manual research limits reach and unsolicited messages may be ignored, but replies can reveal a concrete task sooner than waiting for asset discovery."},"firstAction":"Verify Senja's official offer, then research an eligible course business and send the initial question through its published business email.","activityTarget":{"quantity":6,"activity":"Research eligible owner-led course businesses and send individually relevant business emails where an appropriate public route exists."},"resources":{"assumedMinutes":90,"preparationMinutes":10,"researchMinutesPerActivity":7,"executionMinutesPerActivity":3,"responseMinutes":20,"activityKind":"Researched contacts","tools":[{"name":"Public web search and company websites","access":"Free/public"},{"name":"Free email account","access":"Free/public"}],"directSpend":0,"constraints":"Resources and zero direct spend are experiment assumptions, not confirmed founder capacity. Use only published business routes and respect opt-outs. Response capacity covers brief qualification and permission-based text;"
                    },"commercialLearning":"Log contact source, delivery status, replies, current task, workaround, authority and buying conditions; track activation separately and label payment confirmed only with transaction evidence.","continueWhen":"During a seven-calendar-day observation window, an owner confirms a current proof task and agrees to evaluate Senja; schedule any activation help or payment follow-through only after separate founder time approval.","adjustWhen":"If replies reveal another buyer or workflow, revise targeting; if silent after the observation window, audit delivery, public-route suitability and message relevance before a permission-based follow-up where appropriate.","stopWhen":"Pause this route if appropriate public access cannot be established or reachable owners consistently describe no relevant task; do not treat a small silent sample as rejection.","channelDescription":"Individually researched emails to published business addresses ask about a current testimonial workflow before offering a Senja evaluation. Later-week execution depends on observed outcomes and separately available founder time."},"alternatives":[{"channel":"Template-led discovery","comparison":{"benefit":"A self-service testimonial-request template could support independent evaluation with less ongoing contact work.","barrier":"Creating a useful asset takes upfront effort, and neither search traffic nor distribution access is established, so qualified evidence may arrive slowly."},"preferWhen":"Prefer this when relevant discovery traffic or a permitted distribution route is verified and buyers repeatedly request collection guidance.","firstAction":"Check public search results and accessible creator communities for recurring testimonial-request questions before building an asset."},{"channel":"Community and ecosystem","comparison":{"benefit":"Use-case communities and course-platform ecosystems could expose repeated workflow questions and offer contextual access to buyers.","barrier":"Participation and partner eligibility require verification, promotion may be restricted, and access-building can delay evidence compared with direct outreach."},"preferWhen":"Prefer this when a relevant community permits useful participation or an ecosystem offers an accessible distribution path; existing-user behavior becomes preferable only if authorized user data reveals a reachable active"
                    ,"firstAction":"Inspect public community rules and course-platform directory requirements, and ask whether authorized existing-user workflow evidence is available."}],"messages":[{"subject":"Finding proof for a course page","body":"Hi [name], I found [verified public observation to research]. When updating your course page, how do you collect or find relevant student testimonials? I'm exploring whether Senja fits this workflow, rather than assuming you need another tool."},{"subject":"Worth exploring?","body":"Hi [name], may I send a brief example of using Senja to organize existing testimonials for a course page? If this is not a current task, no problem; knowing your present approach would still help me assess fit."}],"positioning":"For course owners collecting or finding student proof for a sales-page update, Senja offers testimonial collection, import and centralized reuse; its fit and commercial value still need buyer validation.","unknowns":["No market research or external verification was performed.","Senja's current paid offer, capabilities, price and checkout require verification.","Founder availability, product access, prospect access and existing-user data access are unconfirmed; none is assumed as an initial dependency beyond the stated resource assumption."
                    ],"recommendationBasis":{"segments":["s1","s3"],"acquisitionChannels":["s3","s4"],"outreachTemplates":["s2","s3"],"firstTenPlaybook":["s1","s2"
                    ],"thirtyDayPlan":["s3","s4"]},"contractVersion":"2"}

